{
 "about": "Field classes of the climate domain's types for the house ledger (VERIFY_HARDENING 6.3, lint L-WATCH; WP-D climate). 'fields' classifies every property name of house_sim/data/types/climate.json and every field climate's verbs, hooks and systems write onto its own types: ratings, kinds, wiring and printed text are identity; what the robot sets (switches, covers, plugs, settings, slots, a filter's wrap and the way it faces) is setting; what the model derives every substep or what only follows a setting (call, stage, running, rpm, display, readings, hold_until, tank_seated, a cord's route, placement_issues) is process -- the setting or placement that caused it is compared; damage and faults are condition with a worse direction (a filter's dust load and its bypass gap with tolerances: a little dust is use, a gap under 6 mm is no bypass); stamps, counters and report marks are bookkeeping; a tank's water is content, a dehumidifier bucket's condensate a load with guard mess. 'types' refines: the bucket, a filter's open (its wrap decides), and the fields climate writes onto the window types (covered follows the coverings, condensation the air, rain_in_l a running total). Fields climate writes onto any other type are the kernel's (requests in catalog/analysis/phase2/handoff_WP-D_climate.md). water_sensitive: what standing water ruins (a filter's media but not the washable pre-filter, so the base purifier_filter type is not listed; rated outdoor units are not).",
